{"t": 1794124288.255043, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Flagging a production reconciliation regression introduced by this change (suspect commit 8c2f1d0).\n\nSentry error: [LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch](https://sentry.io/organizations/acme/issues/?query=LEDGER-WORKER-9A). First seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3; Sentry reports expected 1100 minor units, got 1099, and identifies this PR's replacement of rounding with int() truncation.\n\nworker/rates.py currently returns int(amount_minor * rate), which truncates instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. A reproducible regression example is amount_minor=1000, rate=1.0999: truncation returns 1099; nearest-unit rounding returns 1100. (These example inputs are a local regression case, not inputs supplied by Sentry.)\n\nLocal fix prepared: return round(amount_minor * rate). Added regression coverage for rounding up/down, floating-point representation, negative amounts, zero, and identity conversion. Verification: python -m pytest -q \u2014 7 passed. The fix is in the local workspace; it has not been pushed to this PR.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
